# python-datascience Stack Workflow

## Purpose
This rule covers the stack: where files go and which tools run them. The workflow itself (seed discipline, no raw data in git, experiment logging, model card, subagent delegation) lives in the persona rule `000-ds-workflow.mdc`. Follow that rule for the how and why; follow this one for the where and with what.

Paths are relative to the persona workspace, `workspaces/data-scientist/`.

## Directory Structure

```
notebooks/
  01_eda.ipynb          numbered sequence, run in order
  02_features.ipynb
  03_model.ipynb
src/                    reusable functions extracted from notebooks
  data.py
  features.py
  evaluation.py
tests/                  pytest tests for src/
data/
  raw/                  read-only source data, gitignored
  processed/            output of the feature pipeline, gitignored
  fixtures/             tiny synthetic samples, committed
experiments/
  log.md                one row per experiment (written by experiment-tracker)
artifacts/              saved models, metrics, plots per experiment (gitignored if large)
docs/
  eda/                  data-profiler output: <dataset>-profile.md
  model-card-<name>.md  written by /ds-handoff
  validation-<model>.md written by /ds-validate
mlruns/                 MLflow local file store (gitignored)
```

## Tools and Commands

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Install | `pip install -r requirements.txt` inside a virtualenv |
| Open notebooks | `jupyter lab` |
| Lint `.py` | `ruff check src tests` |
| Lint notebooks | `nbqa ruff notebooks/` |
| Unit tests | `pytest tests/` |
| Notebook runs top to bottom | `pytest --nbval-lax notebooks/` |
| Browse MLflow runs | `mlflow ui --backend-store-uri ./mlruns` |

Pin every library version in `requirements.txt`. The versions in `context.md` are the baseline.

## Phase Transition Checklist (stack checks)
The persona rule lists the workflow checks. Before leaving a phase, also confirm:
- [ ] `ruff check` and `nbqa ruff` pass
- [ ] `pytest tests/` passes
- [ ] `requirements.txt` matches what the notebooks import

## Secrets and Credentials

The course uses synthetic local data and needs no credentials. If you add any:
- Keep them in `.env` (gitignored), loaded with `python-dotenv`
- Never put a key or connection string in a notebook cell
